  <constraints>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-section-8">Test-modifying override: unconditional FULL rigor + unconditional Step 9.5 quality gates. If any deletion under `tests/integration/{auth,regression,data-mutation,tenant}/**` is proposed (unlikely here — these tests are in `src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/`, not integration paths), same-PR replacement required per FR-B06.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests are KEEP-path protected. Any deletion requires §6.5-documented rationale + reviewer sign-off. DO NOT silently delete failing tests to make CI green — that's the exact anti-pattern the whole test-strategy ADR exists to prevent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="test-diet-classification">Per ADR-038 §7 (build-vs-maintain criteria), classify each failing test: MAINTAIN (fix the test) / DELETE (test was scaffolding, drop) / AMBIGUOUS (reviewer judgment). Document classification per test in task notes. If the test is MAINTAIN, fix it (either update test expectations to match new prod code, OR update prod code to honor test's contract, per root-cause).</constraint>
    <constraint source="§6.5">Silent violation of any ADR rule FORBIDDEN. If the investigation reveals an ADR conflict (e.g., the test asserts an invariant that a later ADR amendment removed), surface via §6.5 path A/B/C — do not silently pick a path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="branch-hygiene">Any master-side changes required (e.g., "the test is correct; master's `CustomerRunGuardModule` regressed on the config-key contract") must be filed as a separate cross-project coordination item — do NOT try to fix master from within this r1 worktree.</constraint>
    <constraint source="INCOMING-doc-§3">INCOMING §3 explicitly warned: "Where the two sides touched different lines of the same file, git merges cleanly and you get master's text sitting beside your shared-tier-premised prose, with no conflict marker." Class B failures may be exactly this failure mode — treat with extra care.</constraint>
  </constraints>

