    <patterns>
      <pattern name="stash-and-compare baseline verification" location="in-session-T220-precedent">
        The technique T220 used to prove pre-existing failures: (a) `git stash push -u -m &lt;unique-tag&gt;` captures inflight changes; (b) capture SHA via `git stash list --format='%H %gs' | head -1`; (c) run test at baseline; (d) `git stash apply &lt;sha&gt;` (never `pop` per worktree shared-stash-stack protocol); (e) find current stash@{n} by tag + `git stash drop stash@{n}`. Same technique will confirm any proposed fix's per-failure impact.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step n="1">Reproduce + document — run `dotnet test src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/` at HEAD. Capture stack traces for each of the 23 failures to `runs/t220-baseline-failure-list-2026-09-29.md` (create the file). Group by failure class (A: FileKvSecretManifestTests × 17; B: CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests × 6).</step>
    <step n="2">Class B investigation (CustomerRunGuardModule) — highest signal for master-merge drift. Read `CustomerRunGuardModule.cs` (master's version, taken during SESSION 23 auto-merge). Compare against pre-master-merge version (SESSION 22 tip). Understand what changed in the config-key contract. Read the 6 failing test bodies; determine per test whether the test asserts an r1-specific contract that master's refactor removed, OR whether master's code regressed on a contract our tests correctly still assert.</step>
    <step n="3">Class A investigation (FileKvSecretManifestTests) — read `FileKvSecretManifest.cs` + the embedded YAML manifest resource. Understand the `KvSecretManifestReadResult.Failure` vs `Success` split. The `A38a_*` prefix suggests these tests were added for auth-v4 A38a work (credential-mode branching). Determine whether the embedded YAML manifest is out of date, the reader logic changed but tests didn't, or the tests assert an r1-specific credential-mode contract master doesn't honor.</step>
    <step n="4">Per-class disposition — for each failure, apply ADR-038 §7 test-diet classification: MAINTAIN (fix test or fix prod) / DELETE (scaffolding) / AMBIGUOUS (owner input). Document classification + rationale in task notes.</step>
    <step n="5">Apply fixes — MAINTAIN cases: implement the fix per root cause (test update or prod update). DELETE cases: remove with rationale + same-PR replacement per FR-B06 if any are under integration paths (they're not; these are unit-test-adjacent). AMBIGUOUS cases: escalate via AskUserQuestion per §6.5.</step>
    <step n="6">Re-run full Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests suite. Goal: 0 failures. If any residual failures, investigate + fix or escalate.</step>
    <step n="7">Re-run full Spaarke.ArchTests suite. MUST stay at 326/326 (no regression from any prod-side changes).</step>
    <step n="8">Regression check adjacent — BFF build clean (0/0). Any other suites that may depend on the modified prod files.</step>
    <step n="9">Step 9.5 quality gates (UNCONDITIONAL) — code-review + adr-check on all modified files.</step>
    <step n="10">Commit + push. Update POML status + TASK-INDEX + current-task.md. Cite §6.5 disposition per failure class in commit message.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Class B investigation reveals master's `CustomerRunGuardModule.cs` regressed on a contract our tests correctly assert — file cross-project coordination item; do NOT attempt to fix master from within this r1 worktree.</trigger>
    <trigger>Class A investigation reveals the embedded YAML manifest resource itself is out of date — coordinate with `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI` project (A38a work owner) before regenerating.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any AMBIGUOUS test-diet classification — MANDATORY owner escalation before delete/maintain decision (per §6.5).</trigger>
    <trigger>Any proposed test deletion would violate ADR-038 KEEP-path — same-PR replacement required; if no natural replacement exists, escalate rather than silently delete.</trigger>
    <trigger>Fix scope discovers changes required to `.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md` beyond the narrow r1 exception note added 2026-09-29 — ADR amendment territory, escalate per §6.5 path B.</trigger>
  </escalation>

