  <notes>
    Test-scope clause per task-create Step 3.5.5b: cover the 23 specific failing tests + regression-check the adjacent test classes (H10SeamsSmoke, DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdaterSmoke, CosmosSmoke) that were passing at baseline. No new test additions unless a fix's root cause reveals a coverage gap.

    §6.5 disposition prediction (author's guess — task-execute may adjust with owner input):
    - Class A most likely: test-updates (embedded YAML manifest changed post-A38a; tests need to update to new canonical secret list)
    - Class B most likely: split — some tests are MAINTAIN (fix by updating test expectations to master's new contract), some may need cross-project coordination (Item 4 §5 territory — model1-*.bicep retirement changes CustomerRunGuardModule config-key semantics)

    Cross-reference with INCOMING §5 Item 4: retiring `model1-*.bicep` may change what `CustomerRunGuardModule` needs to validate. Task 221 execution SHOULD wait until Items 1-4 land, so the config-key contract is stable. Consider deferring Class B fix to post-Item-4.

    Task 221 execution guidance: consider tackling Class A first (independent of Items 1-4) + Class B after Items 1-4 land (when config-key contract is stable). Two-phase execution acceptable if noted.

    COMPLETED 2026-10-05 (session 36, during T242b step 6 — merging to master would have put these failures on master).
    Class A (17 FileKvSecretManifestTests) was fixed by T226. Class B (the 6 CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests):
    root cause = lost code, not stale tests. Commit 3d60b9e59 (REG-02 + REG-05, 2026-08-27) made the guard default ON,
    dropped the TenantId requirement, fell back to DataverseEnvironmentRegistry:AdminEnvironmentUrl and cross-checked the
    two admin URLs; a later master merge (9480f9c4e, via unified-access-control-r2) kept #847's version of
    CustomerRunGuardOptions/Module — the managed-identity half of the same change — and silently dropped the rest.
    Restored on top of #847's credential code. Found alongside: the L2 Api module never emitted
    DataverseEnvironmentRegistry__AdminEnvironmentUrl although REG-07 makes the Api host require it, nor a
    CustomerRunGuard switch although the Api acquires the lock the Worker releases — controlplane-app-service.bicep now
    takes adminDataverseEnvironmentUrl + customerRunGuardEnabled (same values as the Worker). Also fixed: the L2 load-test
    fixture (same REG-07 gap). ControlPlane tests 2113/2114 (0 failed), LoadTests 5/5, ArchTests 349/349.
  </notes>

